{
  "name": "How to Plan Your Interior Restoration Project Successfully",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Planning a successful interior restoration project is all about being organized and knowing what to expect. Think of it like this: Step 1: Define Your Vision. Before anything else, really nail down what you want. What's the new purpose of the room? What style are you going for? What materials do you love? Step 2: Consult with the Pros. Reach out to a qualified contractor, like us at HH Remodeling LLC, who can help you translate your ideas into a realistic plan, including measurements, layouts, and initial design concepts. We’ll discuss the scope and what's possible. Step 3: Material Selection. This is where you pick out all the finishes – flooring, paint colors, cabinetry, fixtures. Do this early! Delays here can really push back your project timeline. Step 4: Demolition & Prep. Once materials are ordered, the physical work begins with clearing out the old and prepping the space for the new. Step 5: Build-Out & Finishes. This is where the magic happens – framing, drywall, tiling, painting, and installing all your chosen elements. Step 6: Final Walkthrough. Inspect the work with your contractor to ensure everything is perfect. A clear plan makes all the difference, so let's get yours started right!",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
